 "script": "France saw five hundred fifty thousand protesters in one day. That's the Interior Ministry's count for Saturday, the AP reported. It began with students blockading schools in mid-September. But the anger spread to prices, as gas, energy and food costs spiked. Then came Limoges. A fire during the unrest destroyed much of its hundred-and-forty-three-year-old town hall. President Macron said there's no place for violence in the Republic. Prices are biting in America too. Gas cost thirty-four percent more in September than a year earlier. What price has risen most where you live? Tell us below.",
